th-academy-id "q-9846" :question/problem "In a trigonometry test, the class instructor decided that students whose $z$-score is greater than or equal to $-1$ will pass the test. The mean percent score $x$ of the students of the class is $\\overset{¯}{x}=64.3%$ with a standard deviation of $\\sigma =5.25%.$ Find the minimum passing score." :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{―}{x}=64.3,$ $z=-1,$ and $\\sigma =5.25$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\  & =64.3+(-1)\\cdot 5.25 \\\\  & =64.3-5.25 \\\\  & =59.05.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the minimum passing score is $59.05%.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-9846/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7e9daa2-4aaa-5c33-b611-231f3d0e4782"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-9846"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-94478/selection/7a9a0f552e5a9574e7415d028d83e4d2bc916f91557b773e49fe3910b966db7d" :answer/id #uuid "e1052c4d-3677-5722-9814-e1ad45329494" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12.4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94478/selection/baa430e1336aa4190f2dfb5cb1447fb3bc99030a868b5f6e116d57288e2e81e9" :answer/id #uuid "5af3d026-1fd3-5ab3-a633-2c4e6c2c8d61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10.1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94478/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "d434e76f-fb36-51e5-9c03-41b91429ca7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-94478/selection/dd068e8faf76584672a35dde6a5fc8f002a6eff7835d53c7a8ce64257406c541" :answer/id #uuid "b44d636f-6eee-5aff