3.6-1.1)\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 10 & =2.5\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, substituting this value back into our first equation and solving for $\\overset{¯}{x},$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}28 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+3.6\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 28 & =\\overset{¯}{x}+3.6\\cdot 4 \\\\ \\overset{¯}{x} & =13.6.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-94478/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "01100ea8-2ab9-511e-8321-6ef5588c4417"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-94478"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-170510/selection/1b562e91f68bc228d59da280605802cc1ce0248d770285443e7d649fb5c75d13" :answer/id #uuid "acf6bbe6-fd3a-545c-9d0f-eedb2a4533ba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170510/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" :answer/id #uuid "8f7fd78c-573c-598c-9c82-1cc1ef62a9b3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170510/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer/id #uuid "34740987-e455-566e-aee5-6ba5b94904a7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170510/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "3577b720-ee3e-57ae-965f-a94b84746281" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170510/selection/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf" :answer/id #uuid "1e3caeac-1f9c-5e17-b4c5-e3b27249a9c3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7.5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-170510/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f88adaa1-07a4-5ba2-8ffb-c8fcb709f11e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-170510/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" :answer-field/choices ["q-170510/selection/1b562e91f68bc228d59da280605802cc1ce0248d770285443e7d649fb5c75d13" "q-170510/selection/0f0db3a18f1d79c4863315eefe754cc5306e04e7aeebf4414ffedb95d6f1bc97" "q-170510/selection/56019ff80d11d678dbd5eca83c729f420f1b6a8ad4259032846618d6b48aa0bc" "q-170510/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-170510/selection/bc6c8e1769ccdd266c8226f86de2176b276b827f8fab68b57be0987a8738f4cf"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-170510" :question/id #uuid "0b0aebfb-96ae-5fa3-a940-5c462fb218ba" :question/math-academy-id "q-170510" :question/problem "A data set has a mean $\\overset{¯}{x}=-100$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=-83$ and $z$-score $z=1.7.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set." :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-83,$ $\\overset{¯}{x}=-100,$ and $z=1.7$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -83 & =-100+1.7\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 17 & =1.7\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =10.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-170510/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2169053d-78fc-5714-82f4-d89fc36ff695"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-170510"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332054/field-1/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" :answer/id #uuid "e1e67dc1-2aa3-58fd-a44e-a79a9b06ad2a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0.8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332054/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6b95bb85-1b21-507b-a856-5875aab59ba6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332054/field-1/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde" :answer-field/choices ["q-332054/field-1/57f27b4de16f64fcab2f3b810a7087fb3b270a063a6807c410b738013ce41fde"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332054" :question/id #uuid "2bb17eba-f9de-5bc3-a770-a3aaaef8ce60" :question/math-academy-id "q-332054" :question/problem "A data set has a mean $\\overset{―}{x}=-2$ and an unknown standard deviation. An observation of the data set has the value $x=-1$ and $z$-score $z=1.25.$ Find the standard deviation of the data set.\n\n$\\sigma =$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=-1,$ $\\overset{―}{x}=-2,$ and $z=1.25$ into the formula and solving for $\\sigma ,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ -1 & =-2+1.25\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ 1 & =1.25\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ \\sigma  & =0.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332054/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "2169053d-78fc-5714-82f4-d89fc36ff695"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332054"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-332274/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer/id #uuid "913cac21-9210-58fe-8219-1c19248d7309" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-332274/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "25f07400-997b-507a-892c-ee9aabd9e516" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-332274/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393" :answer-field/choices ["q-332274/field-1/12b7d840a997b0af25896f37c76d366155c72a970c1525c62ec119b69786f393"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-332274" :question/id #uuid "f03f2caf-4780-58ac-bbd3-6959554865f5" :question/math-academy-id "q-332274" :question/problem "In a certain video game, the mean score of all players is $\\overset{¯}{x}=10$ points with a standard deviation of $1.5$ points. A particular player's $z$-score is $z=2.$ Find this player's score $x.$\n\n$x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "To compute the value of an observation $x$ which yields a given $z$-score in a data set with mean $\\overset{―}{x}$ and standard deviation $\\sigma ,$ we can use the following formula:\n\n$$\nx=\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma \n$$\n\nSubstituting $\\overset{―}{x}=10,$ $z=2,$ and $\\sigma =1.5$ into the formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\overset{―}{x}+z\\cdot \\sigma  \\\\ x & =10+2\\cdot 1.5 \\\\ x & =10+3 \\\\ x & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-332274/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d7e9daa2-4aaa-5c33-b611-231f3d0e4782"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-332274"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
